Title: Signal and Salvage
Order: 1
Production Code: 1x01

EXT. DEBRIS FIELD - OUTER HULL OF THE CAEL LOOM - SHIP'S VIEWPORT

AMB: hull creaks, distant static on an open channel

Read aloud when the party's viewport first clears the debris:

"The Loom fills the whole forward window before you're ready for it — a ring the size of a small moon, dark except where the light catches old metal. Six weeks ago this was a legend. Today you're the first ship here."

[[Cass Ibarra]] holds the helm steady. [[Thistle]] is already still in the way that means they're listening to something the instruments aren't picking up.

THISTLE
(quiet)
It's not silent. Not the way dead things are silent.

CASS IBARRA
Comforting.

[[Nine]] has the salvage arm extended before anyone tells them to.

NINE
Wreckage field, forty meters out. Old. Not Loom-old — recent enough to still have edges.

SFX: a servo whine, then a soft mechanical clunk

GM note: Nine recovers [[the Chord Key]] here — see world/timeline/the-chord-key-recovered.md. Let the player describe finding it; don't over-narrate the object's importance yet.

NINE (CONT'D)
(examining it)
This hums when the Loom does. That's not a coincidence I like.

[[Rell]] watches the debris field through the scope without comment — the player alone knows what's actually going through Rell's head right now; nothing in the scene should tip that to the table.

A small, old, unregistered craft drifts into scanner range, running no beacon.

MEV-KESH (V.O.)
(over comms, unhurried)
You found something. Good. Don't let the others see it first.

MUSIC: IN - low, patient, unresolved

Boxed text for first contact with [[Mev-Kesh]]:

"She doesn't introduce herself right away. She looks at each of you like she's already read most of what she needs to. When she finally speaks again, it's not to explain — it's to warn."

MEV-KESH
Every faction in the Verge heard the same signal you did. Some of them are already three days out. Whatever you do with what you just found, decide before they arrive.

She gives them nothing further — no name for the Loom's builders, no promise of safety. Just the warning, and the silence after it.

MUSIC: OUT

GM note — contingencies: if the party doesn't search the debris field at all, don't force it — Mev-Kesh can simply hand the Chord Key over herself during this same conversation, with less explanation, and let the party wonder why. If the party is hostile or fires on Mev-Kesh's ship, she withdraws immediately without retaliating and doesn't reappear until she chooses to — she's not combat-tested and won't pretend otherwise, but she also won't forget it.
